===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Something added.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1614|author=w:Francis Bacon|chapter=A Letter to the King touching Peacham’s Cause. January 27. 1614|title=Resuscitatio, or, Bringing into publick light severall pieces of the works {{...}} of Francis Bacon|location=London|publisher=William Lee|year_published=1657|page=49|url=http://name.umdl.umich.edu/A28378.0001.001
|passage=For having received, from my ''Lord'', an '''''Additional''''', of great Importance; which was, that ''Owen'', of his own Accord, after Examination, should compare the Case of your ''Majesty'', (if you were Excommunicate,) to the Case, of a Prisoner, Condemned at the Barr; which '''''Additional''''' was subscribed by one Witness; but yet I perceived it was spoken aloud, and in the Hearing of others; I presently sent down a Copy thereof {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1692|author=[[w:Anthony Wood (antiquary)|Anthony à Wood]]|title=Athenæ Oxonienses|location=London|publisher=Thomas Bennet|page=248|url=http://name.umdl.umich.edu/A71277.0001.001
|passage={{...}} having been well vers’d in British Histories, and a singular lover of Antiquities, [he] made many '''additionals''' to the ''Historie of Cambria'' published by ''Dav. Powell'' {{...}}}}

